@@OLD
prior finding. A manifest field line is decided by its label and must be
written `- **Class:**` or `- **Severity:**`, its value the text after that
label only; a finding, a field or a heading the pass cannot read is refused by
name, never dropped.
@@NEW
prior finding. A manifest field line is decided by its label and must be a
dash, whitespace and `**Class:**` or `**Severity:**`, its value the text after
that label only. A field line, a Finding heading or a line that looks like one
that the pass cannot read is refused by name, and so is a manifest from which
it reads no finding; a Class or Severity line outside a finding is prose only
while nothing since the last heading can hold a finding's record.
@@END
